cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "amt-runner: run the AMT.engine pipeline on a Turtle file"
abstract: >-
  amt-runner is a small wrapper script around AMT.engine. It clones the engine
  into a local cache, installs its dependencies once and runs the full
  pipeline (SHACL validation, fuzzy-logic reasoning, consistency check, export
  to Turtle, Cypher, CSV and an interactive HTML graph, plus a run report) on a
  single Turtle file, writing every run into its own folder.
